{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1380875-how-powerful-the-changing-breeds-of-the-first-time-are","id":1380875,"title":"How powerful the Changing Breeds of the First Time are?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-12T23:47:47-07:00","id":1380875,"title":"How powerful the Changing Breeds of the First Time are?","content":"Iirc changing breeds achieved a lot in the First Time and left many great legends, defeating Talons of Wyrm, killing Maeljin Incarnas, etc<br /> <br /> So how powerful are they? Do they have any significant difference from their modern des<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">cedants? Like can wield 6+ traits except Physicals, have 10+ permanent Rage or Gnosis at most?</span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or just knowing many ancient and powerful but now-forgotten powers/artifacts? In one of Endings you will back to the First Time to study Rites of Waking Moon and so on from the elders of the First Tribe</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:36:19-07:00","id":1381224,"title":"","content":"You can kill Maeljin in the present day; it generally relies more on achieving a difficult, non-combat objective.<br /> <br /> As for the other factors, modern Changers tend to have a lot more power than one might consider. Gifts all stack together, after all, and then there are the effects that add permanent Renown dots to tests. If you have 10 dots of Honor, you will wipe the floor with your enemies if using Fu Xi's Honor/Rage of the Nest Mother, because you get to add that on to all of your physical Attributes for a scene. Plenty of other stuff gets tucked away, too; the Numen background in Player's Guide to Garou, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T10:31:31-07:00","id":1381948,"title":"","content":"I think you can get ideas from the Pangaea Realm. Maybe the greatest advantage is environment: more supply (Gnosis, Caerns, unified shapechangers, more mysterious powers and so on), more resistance to silver, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T12:43:16-07:00","id":1382225,"title":"","content":"Some of those capabilities might hold, but the children of two Garou are almost definitely still infertile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T12:57:55-07:00","id":1382226,"title":"","content":"I would hold that mechanically things are the same for the PCs. No 6+ or 11+ statistics. It's just that in the Old Days when the Realm and Umbra were one, that lot more things were possible because the &quot;logic&quot; of myth is in place as opposed to the logic of a mechanistic universe. In myth, it is possible to fly to the sun, steal the moon, or to shoot arrows into the sky where they stick so you can climb them like a ladder. In that kind of world, it is entirely possible to do things that are completely impossible to do later.<br /> <br /> However, that kind of world doesn't exist anymore for a variety of reasons (one of which, I believe, is that as the great deeds of legend were done, it helped cement certain rules of reality, and as more were done, there were more and more rules of how things were).<br /> <br /> I don't think it's really possible to simulate in a game how the world worked in the earliest days. At best, you'd have to use some kind of diceless system with a really great ST and use lots of inspiration from Runequest during their heroquesting examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:12:29-07:00","id":1384852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1380875-how-powerful-the-changing-breeds-of-the-first-time-are?p=1382226#post1382226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hold that mechanically things are the same for the PCs. No 6+ or 11+ statistics. </div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but another question,do you think the legendary shapeshifter heroes have superman traits?<br /> <br /> Like Shu-Horus who almost killed Set, Silver Fang twins who killed that Zmei, or that Khan elder who killed the Yama King? <br /> <br /> Some gifts can manifest them (Mythic Walking), but it seems that they\u2019re still limited to 5 dots in traits? Obviously we can\u2019t get canon stats of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T10:43:17-07:00","id":1384873,"title":"","content":"Same answer as how powerful are Methusalahs.<br /> <br /> no matter the game, edition, or fiction your are doing. the answer is the same. however powerful you need them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-30-2020, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T12:05:52-07:00","id":1384887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1380875-how-powerful-the-changing-breeds-of-the-first-time-are?p=1384852#post1384852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but another question,do you think the legendary shapeshifter heroes have superman traits?<br /> <br /> Like Shu-Horus who almost killed Set, Silver Fang twins who killed that Zmei, or that Khan elder who killed the Yama King?<br /> <br /> Some gifts can manifest them (Mythic Walking), but it seems that they\u2019re still limited to 5 dots in traits? Obviously we can\u2019t get canon stats of them</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Garou all lived in what is clearly the historical level, so they should have the same limitations as any Garou character today. I'd just say they were much more likely to have exceedingly good scores. (Although it you are somehow manifesting a Legendary Garou, it's possible you don't get the actual Garou at the peak but a representation of their mythic stature &quot;preserved&quot; in the Legendary Realm or Tribal Homeland.)<br /> <br /> But in terms of practice in games, I think the question is how do you handle those stats for characters in game? There are two general approaches players and STs can do. The first is that characters can level up their characters to all maximum traits because that's what the game allows. So if you have a trait that starts at 1, you can level up to 5 as long as you have XP. And the ST assigns traits to NPCs to reflect that and keep the PCs in check. The other approach is that a trait at rank 5 really represents the utmost of human elite. If you are not an Olympic level athlete, you shouldn't have a Physical Attribute at 5, or Athletics of 5. If you're not an Einstein or Feynman, you shouldn't have Intelligence of 5 and Science of 5. In this kind of game, the ST keeps things at a more realistic level, and PCs have much work on their part to justify XP spending on certain traits at high levels.<br /> <br /> In reality, most games seem to be in the first category with very few in that second category. In long term LARPS or online games for example, someone can play every game yet not do anything - but if they do it long enough they get enough XP to be among the most bad ass characters. That can be great fun, but the end result is many characters at heavily inflated stats. As a result, if you do somehow encounter that legendary Garou, they're actually not that impressive because EVERYONE reaches that level. If that is the case, I'd give those characters added stats simply in order to distinguish them over the Bone Gnawer janitor who just also happens to have equivalent stats to World Record holding Olympians who is also one of the world's top brain surgeons and best stunt drivers and one of the elite computer hackers. Because if you don't distinguish such legendary characters, there's nothing special about them and therefore there shouldn't be anything special about their accomplishments. And that would lead to a very lame and disappointing story.<br /> <br /> But in my chronicles, where I try for a more realistic distribution of trait levels and require my PCs to justify their XP spending, I'd keep them within the standard 5 traits. That's because such legendary characters CAN still be distinguished from ordinary Garou (although perhaps not to the top tier of Garou heroes today who should have comparable stats).<br /> <br /> I think you should adjust things as needed for your chronicles.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}